<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/html-entities.dtd">

<topic 
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" 
	xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
	title="Quick start" id="Quick-start">

    <var name="version" value="2025.3"/>

    <p>The current version of %instance% (%version%) provides the <a href="linters.md">linters</a> that let you analyze
        Java, Kotlin, Groovy, PHP, JavaScript, TypeScript, C#, Visual Basic, C, C++, Python, and Golang projects. You can
        also extend the default linter configuration using various <a href="features.topic">features</a>. </p>

    <p>As an example, this section explains how you can quickly start working with %instance% using:</p>

    <list>
        <li><a anchor="quickstart-run-in-ide">JetBrains IDEs</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="quickstart-run-using-cli">Command-line interface</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="quickstart-run-in-github">GitHub Actions</a></li>
    </list>

    <chapter title="Prerequisites" id="quickstart-prerequisites">

        <note>You can skip the prerequisites if you would like to run %instance% in <a anchor="quickstart-run-in-ide">JetBrains IDEs</a>.</note>

        <title>
            Set up your project in %cloud%
        </title>
        <link-summary>
            Learn how you prepare your project for using %product%.
        </link-summary>
        <p>Before running Qodana, you need to create a new <a href="cloud-organizations.topic">organization</a> and
            <a href="cloud-projects.topic">project</a> in <a href="https://qodana.cloud">%cloud%</a>. This setup process
            will guide you through
            configuring your project for various <a href="ci.md">CI/CD pipelines</a> and local execution using <a
                    href="https://github.com/JetBrains/qodana-cli">Qodana CLI</a> or
            <a href="qodana-ide-plugin.md">JetBrains IDEs</a>, and will generate a <a href="project-token.md">project
                token</a> required by Qodana linters. Additionally,
            %product% requires a connection to your repositories to track <a href="contributors.md">active
                contributors</a>, as specified by our
            <a href="https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/agreements/qodana/license/">license agreement</a>.</p>
        <note>
            To provide correct work of the contributor counting functionality, add the IP address range
            54.76.32.8/32 to a list of allowed inbound connections on your side.
        </note>
        <note>
            <p style="note">The linters available under the Community, Ultimate, and Ultimate Plus licenses may vary.
                More details can be found in the <a href="pricing.md" anchor="pricing-linters-licenses">Pricing
                    Model</a> section.</p>
        </note>
        <p>If you plan to run the <a href="github.md">Qodana Scan</a> GitHub action on a GitHub-hosted repository, you
            will need to authorize the
            <code>%cloud%</code> GitHub App during the project setup. If you do not have access to the repository that
            you intend to analyze,
            request the necessary access and wait for approval before proceeding. In other cases, you will receive
            instructions and
            configuration snippets that will help you start %product% in your project.</p>
        <p>The project setup uses information from your JetBrains account, which includes licenses and companies.</p>
        <chapter title="Global configurations" id="global-configurations">
            <p>During the project setup stage, you can choose a <a href="global-configuration.md">global
                configuration</a> that will be used while
                analyzing your code.</p>
            <!-- What does this mean ? Does this have to be saved on a repository ? -->
        </chapter>

        <p>To run %instance% in the CLI and GitHub, you will be using a project token available after creating a %cloud%
            <a href="cloud-projects.topic">project</a>. To learn more about it, see the <a href="project-token.md"/> section.</p>

    </chapter>

